From 5416f7876a1f16c67c62102da34f7aa66222e18e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:12:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: discover WebTransport peers with bounded fallback policy

Advertise NODE_WEBTRANSPORT only for actual, derivable UDP listeners.
Try advertised peers with a bounded automatic handshake timeout, then
retain the existing address transport: wss for NET_WSS, raw TCP for IPs.
Explicit wt:// peers remain WT-only. Honor off/prefer/only, proxies and
onlynet, and record one addrman attempt across transport retries.

Cache real failures by exact endpoint in a 4096-entry monotonic TTL/LRU
cache. Do not extend expiry on lookup or cache cancellation/proxy skips.
Expose cache size and reason counters through getwebtransportinfo and the
existing metrics registry. Use actual IPv4/IPv6 family for private-address
proxy checks in the existing raw/WS paths as in WT.

Focused Chronik-enabled daemon/unit builds pass (116 diagnostic daemon
plus 39 corrected daemon actions; 178 unit actions). Ten selected unit
cases pass 319 assertions. The new fallback functional passes automatic
WT success, stale-bit timeout/wss fallback, negative-cache reuse, proxy
no-UDP and only-mode checks; existing WS discovery/address-version tests
pass unchanged. No broad sweep or benchmark was run. W8-W12 and the
fingerprint/proxy acceptance extension remain incomplete; defaults off.

Coordinator ordered integration (2026-10-20):
Existing causal fixes and mechanical namespace/format adaptations are folded at their first responsible owner. Exact inputs and prefix adaptations are recorded in integration-next final delivery; original author provenance is retained.
